ID: vr-74
Title: Make performance-only behavior an immutable creation-time opt-in
Status: DONE
Milestone: Creation-time performance-only opt-in, normal heads unchanged
Dependencies: vr-73
Purpose:
  Owner clarifies that performance-only behavior must be explicitly selected
  when creating a head, not enabled on a normal head or offered as its toggle.
Tasks:
  Add default-off creation checkbox and CLI flag, strict immutable startup
  configuration, read-only manager identity and no live performance toggle.
  Keep opacity customization and existing sleep implementation. Qualify normal
  and opted-in heads, creation forwarding and rejected live policy changes.
  Update authored docs/journal/tracking and only owned live runtime.
Acceptance criteria:
  Omitted flag creates a normal head with no performance switch/dimming.
  Explicit creation opt-in sleeps at10% and speaks at100%; mode cannot be
  changed through live settings. Both preserve normal opacity controls.
  Existing current head is normal; sibling processes/state remain untouched.
Completion evidence:
  .local/qualification/creation-performance-ui-01: twelve actual manager DOM
  checks, including unchecked default, explicit forwarding, next-creation
  reset and read-only identity. Twenty focused session/HTTP cases plus one
  CLI create/host regression, seven Node runner cases and nine book tests pass.
  creation-performance-native-01: actual normal and performance-only Claire,
  four presentations each. Normal retains cursor polling/redraws and selected
  opacity; performance-only has zero sampled sleeping draws/uploads/polls.
  Both reject live policy changes and exercise actual decoded WAV plus real
  face/voice preparation/playback/cancellation. Not a new CPU/listening claim.
  live-creation-performance-01: old owned manager293308/head306520 gracefully
  replaced by306384/305416, normal mode. All controls except the intentionally
  removed performance toggle and all appearance choices preserved. No other
  sessions changed; sixteen promoted source/test files match qualification.
  Candidate .local/worktrees/performance-optin-74 atc6ae6d9.
  Shared pinned model/node_modules inputs are not OS-enforced read-only.
  Qualification uses synthetic input and separate profile/cache/backend.
